    "created_at": "2026-01-05T19:21:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T19:23:35Z",
    "body": "I think that it should be. Currently, none of the browsers have any way of distinguishing, for Reporting API purposes ([NEL, specifically](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#determine-the-network-partition-key) that relies on [determine network partition key](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#determine-the-network-partition-key)), between two processes (or just two different tabs) that has the same origin stuff, but different end point configurations.\n\nThis can be seen in a test currently written in gecko [here](https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277219) which means that, two different tabs or iframes (the test uses iframes), can pollute each other's endpoints, because the keying is not unique enough. It needs to be more unique, than effectively just top level origin for things like Reporting API (or at least NEL).",
